KEDA

KEDA stands for  kubernetes Event driven Autoscaling  

This is a component that allows kubernetes workloads to scale based on external event metrics 

We already use HPA to scale application pods based on CPU utilization . KEDA can extend this approach to event-driven workloads

          Customer places orders
                    |
                    v
             Orders enter queue
                    |
                    v
              KEDA monitors
              queue length
                    |
                    v
          Kubernetes scales Pods
                    |
          +---------+---------+
          |         |         |
          v         v         v
        Pod 1     Pod 2     Pod 3
          |         |         |
          +---------+---------+
                    |
                    v
             Process orders

The current Order management service must support a suitable event source before we can use a queue-based scaling 

KEDA can also use supported external metrics sources, depending on the workload and configuration.

__________________________________________________________________________

KEDA does not automatically replace your existing  HPA. For  a workload managed by a KEDA ScaleObject , KEDA generally creates and manages an HPA based on the configured trigger .We must therefore  avoid creating conflicting autoscaling controllers for the same deployment

Means we should either do HPA  or KEDA

Important: Your current Order Management service does not automatically become queue-driven just because KEDA is installed. We would need to integrate a supported message queue and configure the application to process queued work.
