KEDA Installation: 
------------------

First Check whether the helm is installed or not:
>> helm --version

If installed .Then add  the KEDA Helm repository 
>> helm repo add kedacore https://kedacore.github.io/charts

* helm repo add registers a chart repository.
* kedacore is the local name we'll use for the repository.
* The URL points to the official KEDA Helm charts.


Update the helm repocd ~/production-ecommerce-k8s

mkdir -p infrastructure/kubernetes/keda/order-worker
>> helm repo update

Check the available KEDA chart Version:
>> helm search repo kedacore/keda

Install KEDA 2.21.0
>> helm install keda kedacore/keda \
  --namespace keda \
  --create-namespace \
  --version 2.21.0

Verify the Installation: 

>> kubectl get pods -n keda

We will get the KEDA operator , metrics API server  and admission webhook to become ready 

