Rabbitmq virtual Host: [vhost]

A RabbitMQ virtual host (vhost) is a logical separation inside a RabbitMQ server that allows you to organize and isolate messaging resources.

Think of RabbitMQ as a building, and virtual hosts as separate rooms inside that building.
Each room can have its own queues, exchanges, bindings, and permissions.


                 RabbitMQ Server
                       |
          +------------+------------+
          |            |            |
          v            v            v
       vhost: /    vhost: /orders  vhost: /payments
          |            |            |
          v            v            v
       Queues       Queues         Queues
          |            |            |
          v            v            v
      General       Order          Payment
      Messages      Messages       Messages

These virtual hosts logically separate messaging resources, even though they belong to the same RabbitMQ server.


What does this mean:
metadata:
  queueName: order-events
  vhostName: "/"

queueName: order-events
This tells KEDA which RabbitMQ queue to monitor.

vhostName: "/"
This tells KEDA which virtual host contains the order-events queue.
In RabbitMQ, / is the default virtual host.


Therefore, your configuration tells KEDA to monitor the order-events queue inside the default virtual host.


